1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,428
Could a yeti really survive in

2
00:00:01,428 --> 00:00:02,449
the Himalayas?

3
00:00:02,961 --> 00:00:03,923
Let's build one.

4
00:00:04,261 --> 00:00:06,327
In Sherpa and Tibetan stories,

5
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:07,314
it's a huge,

6
00:00:07,314 --> 00:00:09,148
hairy walker of the high snow.

7
00:00:09,578 --> 00:00:10,867
But a big body sinks in

8
00:00:10,867 --> 00:00:11,795
deep snow.

9
00:00:11,807 --> 00:00:12,980
So you grow wide,

10
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:13,896
furry feet,

11
00:00:13,909 --> 00:00:15,289
like a snowshoe hare.

12
00:00:15,302 --> 00:00:16,521
They spread your weight,

13
00:00:16,521 --> 00:00:17,843
so you stay on top.

14
00:00:18,007 --> 00:00:19,098
But the air up here is

15
00:00:19,098 --> 00:00:19,724
thin.

16
00:00:19,992 --> 00:00:21,188
So you tune your body for

17
00:00:21,188 --> 00:00:22,093
low oxygen,

18
00:00:22,093 --> 00:00:23,114
like the yak,

19
00:00:23,196 --> 00:00:24,520
whose genes are built for high

20
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:25,308
altitude.

21
00:00:25,936 --> 00:00:27,202
But then winter comes,

22
00:00:27,202 --> 00:00:28,513
and there's nothing to eat.

23
00:00:29,025 --> 00:00:30,244
So you sleep through it,

24
00:00:30,244 --> 00:00:31,439
like a brown bear,

25
00:00:31,521 --> 00:00:33,412
living on stored fat for months.

26
00:00:34,319 --> 00:00:35,688
Now look at what you built.

27
00:00:36,118 --> 00:00:36,652
A big,

28
00:00:36,652 --> 00:00:37,569
furry bear.

29
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,461
In twenty seventeen,

30
00:00:39,508 --> 00:00:41,864
scientists tested nine yeti samples.

31
00:00:42,295 --> 00:00:43,443
One was a dog.

32
00:00:43,711 --> 00:00:45,521
The other eight were Asian bears.

33
00:00:45,859 --> 00:00:47,275
And the name yeti comes from

34
00:00:47,275 --> 00:00:49,178
Tibetan words meaning rock bear.

35
00:00:49,609 --> 00:00:51,187
So the legend isn't empty.

36
00:00:51,269 --> 00:00:53,045
It grew from a real animal.

